{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-10773-r4516398","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Tahini Goddess Dressing","sourcePageId":10773,"sourceRevision":"4516398","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-20T02:54:40Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Tahini%20Goddess%20Dressing&oldid=4516398","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:11.956Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for salad dressing","Category:Recipes using canola oil","Category:Recipes using chive","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using tahini","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"adcc6cfac51eea56476d19e6db05d0664613aab6f40dbcb01bf8d42dca8ead52","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Salad dressing recipes\n| Yield = About 24 oz\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nThis '''tahini goddess dressing''' is similar to several commercial brands. It is excellent on salad and rice or as a marinade.  \n\n== Ingredients ==\n*1⅓ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Canola Oil|canola oil]]\n* ⅔ cup water\n*6 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Tahini|tahini]]\n*6 tbsp [[Cookbook:Cider vinegar|cider vinegar]]\n*4 tbsp [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n*5 tbsp [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n*6 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* ⅛ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Xanthan gum|xanthan gum]]\n\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Sesame Seed|sesame seeds]], toasted\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Chive|chives]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# In a [[Cookbook:Blender|blender]], combine the oil, water, tahini, vinegar, lemon juice, soy sauce, garlic, and xanthan gum. Blend on high for about 2 minutes. You will see a change in the texture of the mixture as the xanthan gum starts to work, producing a very smooth, creamy appearance.\n# Add the sesame seeds, parsley, and chives. Blend on low, just until mixed.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* Xanthan gum is available in many grocery stores in the baking or grain sections.\n* Be careful with the xanthan gum; too much and the mixture will turn into a rubbery glob, too little and the oil and water will separate.\n* If brand substitutions are made, the recipe may need adjustment. \n* This dressing has a very strong flavors that need to be balanced. When in balance, the flavor really explodes.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for salad dressing]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tahini]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chive]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using canola oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Tahini Goddess Dressing","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1⅓ cup canola oil","sourceText":"1⅓ cup canola oil","amountText":"1⅓ cup canola oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"⅔ cup water","sourceText":"⅔ cup water","amountText":"⅔ cup water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"6 tbsp tahini","sourceText":"6 tbsp tahini","amountText":"6 tbsp tahini","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"6 tbsp cider vinegar","sourceText":"6 tbsp cider vinegar","amountText":"6 tbsp cider vinegar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"4 tbsp lemon juice","sourceText":"4 tbsp lemon juice","amountText":"4 tbsp lemon juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"5 tbsp soy sauce","sourceText":"5 tbsp soy sauce","amountText":"5 tbsp soy sauce","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"6 cloves garlic","sourceText":"6 cloves garlic","amountText":"6 cloves garlic","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"⅛ tsp xanthan gum","sourceText":"⅛ tsp xanthan gum","amountText":"⅛ tsp xanthan gum","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"2 tbsp sesame seeds, toasted","sourceText":"2 tbsp sesame seeds, toasted","amountText":"2 tbsp sesame seeds, toasted","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"2 tbsp parsley","sourceText":"2 tbsp parsley","amountText":"2 tbsp parsley","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-11","name":"2 tbsp chives","sourceText":"2 tbsp chives","amountText":"2 tbsp chives","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"In a blender, combine the oil, water, tahini, vinegar, lemon juice, soy sauce, garlic, and xanthan gum. Blend on high for about 2 minutes. You will see a change in the texture of the mixture as the xanthan gum starts to work, producing a very smooth, creamy appearance.","sourceText":"In a blender, combine the oil, water, tahini, vinegar, lemon juice, soy sauce, garlic, and xanthan gum. Blend on high for about 2 minutes. You will see a change in the texture of the mixture as the xanthan gum starts to work, producing a very smooth, creamy appearance.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Add the sesame seeds, parsley, and chives. Blend on low, just until mixed.","sourceText":"Add the sesame seeds, parsley, and chives. Blend on low, just until mixed.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:10773","recordId":"wikibooks-10773-r4516398","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4516398","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Tahini%20Goddess%20Dressing&oldid=4516398","sourceSha256":"adcc6cfac51eea56476d19e6db05d0664613aab6f40dbcb01bf8d42dca8ead52","parserVersion":"wikibooks-sections-v3","quantityParserVersion":"source-prefix-v2","license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"reviewStatus":"source-extracted-unreviewed","changeNotice":"Source-language section extraction; markup removed. Not culinarily reviewed, translated or runtime-approved.","recipe":{"name":"Tahini Goddess Dressing","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1⅓ cup canola oil","sourceText":"1⅓ cup canola oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null,"